       For each unique orbit position (r,c) with r <= c and r+c <= side-1 (upper-left triangle),
       decide fg/bg; propagate to all 4 rotated positions with the same color.
       Use body_color for most orbits, accent_color for 1-2 orbits (typically outermost).
       Ensure 50-75% fill.
    3. Classify each size-4 orbit as full or partial. Inner orbits (closer to center) -> full;
       outer orbits -> partial. Ensure >=1 partial orbit exists.
    4. For each partial orbit, keep exactly 1 of 4 rotated positions; choose from a consistent
       sector (e.g., pick one rotation index 0-3 and use it for most partial orbits).
    5. Place the square at a random valid position in the 10x10 grid (>=1 margin all sides).
    6. Write the retained pixels (full orbits + 1 pixel per partial orbit) onto a bg grid -> input.
    7. Verify solver recovers the intended output (unique smallest rotation-consistent square).
